   "source": [
    "How we can use the model? Suppose that given the data we want to estimate how much will be the Life expectancy for the Spendings of $1000$? The answer is we plug $x=1000$ into the model that we trained on the data and get the predicted answer"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "collapsed": false,
    "jupyter": {
     "outputs_hidden": false
    },
    "pycharm": {
     "name": "#%%\n"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "The Life expectancy for x=1000 is 76.0385597477357\n",
      "The Life expectancy for x=20000 is 106.11185527971398\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "def get_prediction(model, x):\n",
    "    return model.coef_[0] * x + model.intercept_\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'The Life expectancy for x=1000 is {get_prediction(lin_model, 1000)}')\n",
    "print(f'The Life expectancy for x=20000 is {get_prediction(lin_model, 20000)}')"
   ]
