     "name": "#%% md\n"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "Let's check the $R^2$ correlation between all the features. For that we will use the method *corr* of the DataFrame, that computes the correlation between all the numerical columns of the DataFrame. As the parameter *name* we pass *pearson* - which stands for the ususal $R^2$. \n",
    "\n",
    "To display the correlation matrix, we use the command *heatmap* of the *seaborn* package"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "pycharm": {
     "name": "#%%\n"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "<Axes: >"
      ]
